# KNOWN GAP (fmt, filed 2026-08-14 from the R42 Track-D brief-review pass 2):
# `gg fmt` drops the trailing comma of a ONE-TUPLE TYPE — `(int,)` in type
# position formats to `(int)`, which is a parenthesized type, not a 1-tuple.
# The VALUE spelling `(5,)` keeps its comma; only the TYPE loses it, so the
# round trip is form-changing (and the re-parsed program may not typecheck).
# INTENDED: the 1-tuple type keeps its comma exactly like the 1-tuple value.
# Cell: type position, var-decl. Siblings not sampled here: 1-tuple type as a
# param type / return type / generic arg (same emitter, unverified).
# Wired test: fmt_one_tuple_type_keeps_comma (tests/integration.rs, #[ignore]d).
void main():
    (int,) t3 = (5,)
    print(t3.0)
